      "message": "A stack frame is \u003e4 bytes, so I wouldn\u0027t expect this to be able to walk the stack for each of the stack pointers.\n\nIs there something the specifies that `get_panic_stack_pointer()` returns a list of stack pointers? From the function name, it just returns a single stack pointer, without any relation to the full stack itself.",
